cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite it as below."
title: "Interstellar Expansion Percolation Model"
authors:
  - family-names: "Ostashewski"
    given-names: "Stan"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-05-31
url: "https://github.com/blazzer/interstellar-expansion-model"
license: MIT
type: software
abstract: >
  A grid-based simulation exploring bounded expansion dynamics for hypothetical
  interstellar civilizations. Models both biological and robotic colonization
  waves under constraints on motivation, coordination, goal coherence, resource
  depletion, and failure cascades - providing a tunable parametric framework
  for exploring conditions under which interstellar expansion remains bounded
  rather than achieving Hart-Tipler galactic colonization.
keywords:
  - "fermi paradox"
  - "interstellar colonization"
  - "agent-based simulation"
  - "astrobiology"
  - "percolation"
  - "bounded expansion"